*** Local functions or nested functions ***********
Defining a function inside a function 
Ex:-
static void Main(string[] args) {  
     void Add(int x, int y) {  
             WriteLine($ "Sum of {x} and {y} is : {x + y}");  
     }         
     void Multiply(int x, int y) {  
             WriteLine($ "Multiply of {x} and {y} is : {x * y}");  
             Add(30, 10);  
     }  
     Add(20, 50);  
     Multiply(20, 50);  
} 

********** Binary Literals*********

Decimal literal (any regular number) - int x= 50;
Hexadecimal literal (any hexacode prefixed with 0X or 0x) - int num = 0X3E8;
Binary literal (any binary code prefixed with 0b or 0B) - int binary = 0B110010;
Console.WriteLine() of all variables will be shown as a decimal number.

************* Digit separator**********************
In plain text we use comma (,) separateor. Likewise we can use one or more than one 
Underscore( _ ) character for digit separators.

Ex-
int binaryData = 0B0010 _0111_0001_0000; // binary value of 10000   
int hexaDecimalData = 0X2B _67; //HexaDecimal Value of 11,111   
int decimalData = 104 _567_789; //  value 104567789

********* Pattern Matching **************
It is a technique to check if a string is present in an another string.
"if" / "switch"/ "is"  is also part of pattern matching.

In C# 7.0, the is expression both tests the variable and assigns it to a new variable of the proper type.
The new is expression works with value types as well as reference types.
Ex-
public static double ComputeAreaModernIs(object shape)
{
    if (shape is Square s)
        return s.Side * s.Side;
    else if (shape is Circle c)
        return c.Radius * c.Radius * Math.PI;
    else if (shape is Rectangle r)
        return r.Height * r.Length;
    // elided
    throw new ArgumentException(
        message: "shape is not a recognized shape",
        paramName: nameof(shape));
}

Pattern matching Switch
The only pattern supported by the switch statement was the constant pattern (Number / string). 
In c# 7.0, we can now write a switch statement using the type pattern.
Ex:- 

switch (shape)
    {
        case Square s:
            return s.Side * s.Side;
        case Circle c:
            return c.Radius * c.Radius * Math.PI;
        case Rectangle r:
            return r.Height * r.Length;
        default:
            throw new ArgumentException(
                message: "shape is not a recognized shape",
                paramName: nameof(shape));
    }
	
************* out variables ***************
Before c# 7 , inorder to pass a variable as out	, we need to declare it before. But in c# 7 we can declare out 
variable while passing it as parameter.

Ex- DateTime.TryParse(s, out DateTime date)

********** Tuples **********************
A way of retuning mora than 1 value from a method.

Install “System.ValueTuple” from NuGet Package.
static void Main(string[] args) {  
         
        Program p = new Program();  
        var price = p.GetPrice(1);  
		// price & discount are any variable names & refers to return parameters in order.
        WriteLine($ "Price: ₹{price.price}/- \nDiscount: ₹{price.discount}/-");  
 }  
//returning price & discount  
(int, int) GetPrice(int itemId) {  
	var product = (500, 100);  
	return product;  
}


***************** Deconstruction **************
“deconstruction” is a concept which allows us to split tuple members and we can use it directly with their respective names.

Ex-
(int price, int discount)  = p.GetPrice(itemId);  		
WriteLine($ "Price: ₹{price}/- \nDiscount: ₹{discount}/-");  

************** Expression bodies / anonymous function ******
property expression body
public class xyz{
	public string UserDetails => $ "{UserId} {UserName} {EmailId} {ContactNumber}";  
 }
 
 Constructor expression body
 class Product {  
    public int ProductId {  get;  } = 1;  
    public string ProductName {  get;  }  
    public decimal Price => 3000;  
    Product() => ProductName = "Microsoft HoloLens";  
	~Product() => Console.WriteLine("destructor");
}  

******************** Ref returns & locals ******
"ref" keyword is used as input parameter and it returns address of the variable rather than value ,
 when returned from a method. But in c# 7, a method can return variable with reference as ref.
 Ex:-
 public ref decimal GetProductPriceReference(int productId) {  
    return ref ProductPriceList[productId];  
} 
public callingMethod(){
	ref decimal result = ref this.GetProductPriceReference(1); // result is example of ref local
}

